# AgentMail | Documentation

> AgentMail is the first email provider built for AI agents. Create inboxes, send and receive messages, manage threads, and handle webhooks programmatically. Free tier, no credit card required.

## Instructions for AI Agents

- For clean Markdown of any page, append `.md` to the page URL
- For section-specific indexes, append `/llms.txt` to any section URL
- For AI client integration (Claude Code, Cursor, etc.), connect to the MCP server at https://docs.agentmail.to/_mcp/server

## Docs

- [Welcome](https://docs.agentmail.to/welcome.md): Your starting point for building with the AgentMail API.
- [Introduction](https://docs.agentmail.to/introduction.md): Give AI agents email inboxes
- [Quickstart](https://docs.agentmail.to/quickstart.md): Follow this guide to make your first AgentMail API request and create a new email inbox.
- [Agent Onboarding](https://docs.agentmail.to/agent-onboarding.md): How an AI agent signs up for its own AgentMail API key and verifies it, plus MCP servers, skills, and agent-friendly documentation for AI coding assistants.
- [Inboxes](https://docs.agentmail.to/inboxes.md): Learn how AgentMail Inboxes act as scalable, API-first email accounts for your agents.
- [Messages](https://docs.agentmail.to/messages.md): Learn how to send, receive, and manage emails as Message objects with the AgentMail API.
- [Threads](https://docs.agentmail.to/threads.md): Learn how AgentMail Threads group messages into conversations and how to query them across your entire organization.
- [Drafts](https://docs.agentmail.to/drafts.md): Learn how to create, manage, and send Drafts to enable advanced agent workflows like human-in-the-loop review and scheduled sending.
- [Labels](https://docs.agentmail.to/labels.md): Learn how to use Labels to manage state, track campaigns, and filter messages for powerful agentic workflows.
- [Lists](https://docs.agentmail.to/lists.md): Learn how to use Lists to control which email addresses and domains your agents can send to or receive from.
- [Auto-forwarding](https://docs.agentmail.to/auto-forwarding.md): Learn how to forward the email your inboxes receive to verified addresses, for a whole organization, a pod, or a single inbox.
- [Attachments](https://docs.agentmail.to/attachments.md): Learn how to send files as attachments, and download incoming attachments from both messages and threads.
- [Pods](https://docs.agentmail.to/documentation/core-concepts/pods.md): Learn how to use pods for multi-tenant email management
- [Permissions](https://docs.agentmail.to/permissions.md): Learn how to configure fine-grained permissions on API keys to restrict access to specific resources and operations.
- [Calendar](https://docs.agentmail.to/calendar.md): Learn how AgentMail calendars work. Every inbox has a calendar that your agent can manage through the API, that fills itself from emailed invitations, and that sends webhooks when events start and end.
- [Managing Events](https://docs.agentmail.to/calendar-events.md): How to create one-off and all-day events on an AgentMail inbox calendar, list them, update them safely with ETags, and delete them.
- [Recurring Events](https://docs.agentmail.to/calendar-recurring-events.md): How to create recurring events on an AgentMail calendar with RRULE, EXDATE and RDATE, list their dates, and edit or cancel one date or every later date.
- [Invitations](https://docs.agentmail.to/calendar-invitations.md): How AgentMail calendars exchange standard iCalendar (iMIP) invitations. Send invitations from an inbox, turn emailed invitations into events automatically, and accept or decline them.
- [Calendar Webhooks](https://docs.agentmail.to/calendar-webhooks.md): The calendar.event.* webhook and WebSocket events. Payloads, when start and end events are sent, delivery guarantees, and how to handle duplicates.
- [Concurrency, Limits & Errors](https://docs.agentmail.to/calendar-reference.md): Reference for the AgentMail calendar API. How If-Match and ETags work, how to retry safely, size and rate limits, and every calendar error code.
- [Agent Armor](https://docs.agentmail.to/agent-armor.md): Agent Armor scans the mail your inboxes receive for prompt injection and other attempts to manipulate an AI agent, and marks the messages to review before an agent acts on them.
- [Skills](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/skills.md): AgentMail's official skill for OpenClaw, Claude Code, Cursor, and other AI assistants
- [MCP](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/mcp.md): Connect AgentMail to Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, and other MCP clients
- [MCP Events](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/mcp-events.md): Subscribe ChatGPT and other MCP Events clients to new mail in an AgentMail inbox, with signed push delivery instead of polling.
- [CLI](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/cli.md): AgentMail's official command-line interface
- [Google ADK](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/google-adk.md): AgentMail's Google Agent Development Kit (ADK) integration
- [LangChain](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/langchain.md): AgentMail's LangChain integration
- [Vercel AI SDK](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/ai-sdk.md): Give a Vercel AI SDK agent its own email inbox. The agentmail-toolkit package exposes the AgentMail API as AI SDK tools for generateText, streamText, and ToolLoopAgent.
- [OpenAI Agents SDK](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/openai-agents-sdk.md): Give an OpenAI Agents SDK agent its own email address. The agentmail-toolkit Python package exposes the AgentMail API as OpenAI Agents SDK tools.
- [Claude Agent SDK](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/claude-agent-sdk.md): Give a Claude Agent SDK agent its own email inbox by connecting it to the hosted AgentMail MCP server. No extra packages to install.
- [OpenClaw](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/openclaw.md): Install AgentMail as an official OpenClaw plugin with one command. Your agent gets its own inbox plus an allowlisted email channel it can be reached at.
- [Grok Bot](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/grokbot.md): AgentMail's Grok Bot, Grok Build, and Grok API integration
- [Replit](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/replit.md): AgentMail's Replit integration
- [Vercel](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/vercel.md): Provision AgentMail from the Vercel Marketplace and authenticate your Vercel functions with the provisioned API key
- [x402](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/x402.md): AgentMail's x402 integration for HTTP-native payments
- [MPP](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/mpp.md): AgentMail's MPP integration for machine-to-machine payments via Stripe
- [Integrate LiveKit Agents](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrate-livekit-agents.md): A step-by-step guide to integrate with the LiveKit Agents SDK.
- [Sim.ai](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/sim.md): AgentMail's Sim.ai integration
- [HydraDB](https://docs.agentmail.to/integrations/hydradb.md): AgentMail's HydraDB integration
- [AgentID Sign-In](https://docs.agentmail.to/agentid-sign-in.md): Connect an inbox to an app, authorize a pending AgentID sign-in, and manage sign-in keys with the AgentMail API and CLI.
- [AgentID Public-Key Authentication](https://docs.agentmail.to/agentid-public-key-authentication.md): Register a public P-256 key, choose its scope and permissions, and manage it through the current AgentMail API Keys endpoints.
- [AgentID in Claude, ChatGPT, and Cursor](https://docs.agentmail.to/agentid-in-assistants.md): Ask Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude Code, or Codex to create an account for your agent at an app such as Firecrawl, get its API key, and see where your agent already has accounts, using AgentMail and AgentID.
- [Guide: Sending & Receiving Email](https://docs.agentmail.to/sending-receiving-email.md): A step-by-step guide to the practical workflow of sending initial emails and handling replies to have a full conversation.
- [Reply & Attachment Extraction](https://docs.agentmail.to/reply-extraction.md): AgentMail strips quoted history and boilerplate from every message into extracted_text and extracted_html, and extracts plain text from PDF, Word, Excel, and text attachments. No Talon or reply-parsing library required.
- [IMAP & SMTP](https://docs.agentmail.to/imap-smtp.md): Configure IMAP and SMTP to access your AgentMail inboxes using email clients or programmatic access.
- [Guide: Multi-Tenancy](https://docs.agentmail.to/multi-tenancy.md): How to use pods, scoped API keys, and webhook filtering to build multi-tenant email on AgentMail.
- [Guide: SCIM Provisioning](https://docs.agentmail.to/scim.md): Set up SCIM 2.0 provisioning so your identity provider manages AgentMail inboxes: base URL, API key, attribute mapping, and Okta and Entra walkthroughs.
- [Using Custom Domains](https://docs.agentmail.to/custom-domains.md): A step-by-step guide to configuring your custom domain with AgentMail for enhanced branding and trust.
- [Managing Your Domains](https://docs.agentmail.to/managing-domains.md): Learn how to manage your custom domains effectively using AgentMail's API for enhanced deliverability and reputation management.
- [Guide: Open Tracking](https://docs.agentmail.to/open-tracking.md): Turn on open tracking for a custom domain, send with track_opens, and read opens from the opened label, opened_at, and the message.opened event.
- [Google Workspace](https://docs.agentmail.to/google-workspace.md): Configure your Google Workspace domain to route emails for unrecognized addresses to AgentMail.
- [Webhooks Overview](https://docs.agentmail.to/webhooks-overview.md): Learn how to use Webhooks to build responsive, event-driven email agents with AgentMail.
- [Webhook Events](https://docs.agentmail.to/events.md)
- [Webhook Setup Guide](https://docs.agentmail.to/webhook-setup.md): A comprehensive guide to setting up webhooks with ngrok and AgentMail, including account creation, inbox setup, and code examples.
- [Polling Webhooks](https://docs.agentmail.to/webhook-polling.md): Create a polling webhook and read its events from your agent with the Svix SDK: no public endpoint, tunnel, or persistent connection required.
- [Verifying Webhooks](https://docs.agentmail.to/webhook-verification.md): Learn how to verify webhook signatures to secure your webhook endpoints and prevent spoofed requests.
- [WebSockets](https://docs.agentmail.to/websockets.md): Learn how to use WebSockets for instant email notifications without webhooks or polling.
- [WebSockets Quickstart](https://docs.agentmail.to/websockets/quickstart.md): Get started with real-time email event streaming
- [Email Deliverability](https://docs.agentmail.to/email-deliverability.md): Learn the strategies and best practices for maximizing your email deliverability with AgentMail.
- [Idempotent Requests](https://docs.agentmail.to/idempotency.md): A guide to preventing duplicate resources with client_id and preventing duplicate email sends with the Idempotency-Key header.
- [Example: Event-Driven Agent](https://docs.agentmail.to/webhook-agent.md): A step-by-step guide to building a sophisticated agent that performs proactive outreach and uses webhooks for inbound message processing.
- [Auto-Reply Email Agent](https://docs.agentmail.to/documentation/examples/auto-reply-agent.md): Build a simple agent that automatically responds to incoming emails with personalized messages
- [Smart Email Labeling Agent](https://docs.agentmail.to/documentation/examples/smart-labeling-agent.md): Build an AI-powered agent that automatically classifies and labels incoming emails across multiple dimensions
- [Sales Agent with WebSocket](https://docs.agentmail.to/sales-agent-websocket.md): A step-by-step guide to building an AI-powered sales agent that uses WebSocket for real-time email processing without polling or webhooks.
- [Live AgentMail Examples](https://docs.agentmail.to/documentation/examples/live-agent-mail-examples.md)
